report=['# Lumen Run 1 investigation', '', recommend, '', '## 1. Run 1 provenance',f'Public portal independently confirms team Lumen, run ID `{p["official_public_run"]["id"]}`, created `{p["official_public_run"]["createdAt"]}`, displayed score 60.1, precision 91%, recall 29%. Difficulty display is easy 40%, medium/observable-hard/ambiguous 0%. The portal explicitly rounds difficulty recalls to the nearest 10%; these are not exact counts or exact zero recall. Local train OOF results are not official test results.','', 'The two designated local upload files are byte-identical to protected V1 and are reproducible from its packaged source. SHA256:',f'- CSV: `{hashlib.sha256((ROOT/"outputs/final_submission/predictions.csv").read_bytes()).hexdigest()}`',f'- Code ZIP: `{hashlib.sha256((ROOT/"outputs/final_submission/lumen_strategy3_v1_code.zip").read_bytes()).hexdigest()}`','Public Run 1 metadata contains no file hash, original filename or artifact download. Therefore exact correspondence between these designated local files and server-uploaded bytes remains unverified; a trusted upload receipt/original-file digest would be required. The supplied login was rejected again when checking receipt access after Run 1 appeared; no passwords were guessed, no account changes were made and no further login attempts were made. The public leaderboard API exposed only run-summary fields used here. See run1_provenance.json.','', '## 2. Exact OOF category audit','Labels and OOF scores are realigned by unique transaction hash. Easy 800, medium 225, observable-hard 200, ambiguous 25; all 38,881 legitimate payments form a common negative background for each category AP. Other positive categories are excluded from that category AP calculation, never relabelled legitimate. Both fraction of all 40,131 transactions and the category-specific AP prevalence/denominator are reported. AP across categories is not directly comparable because prevalence differs.','',md(friendly),'','Recall is measured in the same global top 402 OOF transactions, not reranked separately within each difficulty. The selected set contains 321 easy, 5 medium and 76 legitimate payments; zero observable-hard and ambiguous positives. Score cutoff is 0.6547633324. Overall pooled AP is 0.5371864804; mean fold AP is 0.5448294042. Pooled precision is 326/402 = 81.0945%, recall 326/1250 = 26.08%. Per-fold review budgets are 134 and are reported separately; mixed-fold OOF scores can have different scales. category_metrics.csv includes each fold and pooled, complete score summaries and group-bootstrap AP intervals (200 pooled / 60 fold replicates, conditional on fitted OOF scores).','', '## 3. Why medium cases lose the review budget','The median medium score is 0.023245, with 95th percentile 0.313557, far below the global 0.654763 cutoff. The median legitimate score is 0.003991. Medium is not ranked below most legitimate activity: median medium score exceeds 89.00% of legitimate scores, and descriptive pairwise AUC is 0.8614. But the median medium case is still outranked by 4,278 legitimate payments. Extreme-tail ranking, not simply a binary 0.5 threshold, is the issue.','', 'All 225 medium rows were explained using their held-out fold model. Each fold was refitted at the original V1 seed, reproducing its saved OOF probabilities exactly (max absolute difference zero); SHAP sums to raw model log-odds. SHAP is an explanation of the fitted model, not causal evidence about laundering intent.','',md(pd.DataFrame(sw)),'', 'Pair-history features give positive evidence to both medium positives and false positives. In contrast, the 5-minute/burst block contributes about -0.052 log-odds on average to medium rows versus +2.692 to selected high-scoring legitimate rows, with the direction consistent across all three folds. The model expected raw-score baseline is around -5.2 to -5.35; that is a SHAP reference logit, not the empirical class-prevalence logit. Medium cases lack sufficient positive boosts to reach the review threshold.','', 'Observable repeated patterns: 75/76 (98.7%) top false positives and 214/225 (95.1%) medium positives are one-off directed pairs, versus 33.8% of legitimate payments overall. One-off status is therefore insufficient to separate intent. Receiver burst >1 appears in 56.6% of high FPs versus 25.8% of medium rows. Five-minute prior-inflow matching within 10% appears in 13/76 high FPs but 0/225 medium rows; later-outflow matching appears in 19/76 high FPs and 0/225 medium rows. These descriptive patterns are conditioned on selected model errors and must not be read as independent causal estimates. No annotation is used as an input.','', '## 4. Repeatable false-positive and false-negative structure','The 76 high-scoring negatives include 16 lawful chain payments, 14 bipartite, 12 aggregate-relay, 9 multi-stage, 8 fan-out-in, 6 cycles, 5 fan-in, 4 stack, 1 distributed-relay and 1 random. This is a recurring lawful-motif tail, not one anomalous account. Family names are annotation-only descriptions; observed pair/burst/flow features establish the behavioural comparison. False-positive rates normalized by family size are in false_positive_family_rates.csv; raw counts alone would overstate the significance of the large relay families.','', 'Among the lowest-scoring 125 positives, 50 aggregate-relay and 42 distributed-relay observable-hard payments plus 19 ambiguous rows account for 111 cases; the remainder are 13 medium and 1 easy. These are recurrent failures of current history representations. Low scores do not prove that the 200 observable-hard cases have no signal. Only the deliberately ambiguous label category is documented as independent of supplied observables. All selected local rows and scores are recorded in local_error_rows.csv for inspection; annotation fields never enter fitting.','', '## 5. Fixed finite experiments','The three candidates were specified in experiment_plan.json after diagnosis and before fitting. Parameters remain V1 CatBoost 1200/depth6/lr .035/L2 10/rsm .85/four CPU threads/seed 20261024. weight3 weights every binary positive by three (no category weights); without5min removes 43 five-minute features plus 2 burst features; flexible_sums adds 33 label-free cumulative-prefix compatibility features with at most 8 chronological events, windows 1h/6h/24h, actual source debit and delivered reference USD. Same-timestamp events are excluded. Compatibility is not exact asset provenance, subset-sum inference or confirmed fund tracing.','',md(comp),'', 'All P/R columns in this comparison use global pooled OOF top402; all_metrics.csv additionally gives every fold top134, wallet top103 and temporal top120. The removal ablation raises medium AP from 2.7149% to 4.4549% and doubles medium catches from 5 to 10, but loses 10 easy catches (321 to 311), reducing total catches from 326 to 321 and mean AP to 51.92%. That is evidence of a tradeoff, not a promotable improvement. Positive reweighting increases typical medium scores without improving their global review-budget rank. Prefix compatibility does not solve the tail separation.','', '## 6. Holdouts, acceptance and uncertainty','A uses the exact original cohort/scenario SGKF folds. B0 uses disjoint supervised wallet endpoint halves while retaining authorized unlabelled context; C fits first-five-day labels and evaluates last-two-day labels using full permitted offline context. Neither is an independent graph test or streaming detection test; some annotation groups can cross B/C. These protocols were already inspected during V2, and there is no independent labelled final release. B1 metrics remain uninspected unless a frozen finalist qualifies; its labels also participated in Track A development.','',json.dumps(accept,indent=2),'','Seed robustness was evaluated only for the frozen new finalist, flexible_sums; the other two already failed primary gates and were not seed-confirmed. A null seed-check value means not evaluated, not a measured negative result. All original promotion requirements remain: >=1 pp mean AP gain, improvement in >=2 folds, paired group-bootstrap lower bound >0, positive confirmation-seed gain, no >2 pp B/C AP regression, then clean raw-source reproduction and artifact compliance. A non-regression check on pooled top402 true-positive count is added; no criterion is relaxed. Paired group intervals use cohort/scenario/background-row blocks, 300 replicates, and condition on fitted predictions, excluding training and selection uncertainty. The same folds have been reused for this finite three-candidate study and previous V2 work; reported gains can still be optimistic.','', '## 7. Recommendation and reproducibility',recommend,'No test predictions for a new run, uploads, submissions, external labels, private test answers, category-derived predictors or label propagation were created or used. Every protected V1/V2 file remains unchanged; verification.json records hashes and independent recalculation of candidate CSV metrics. A rejected candidate is not exported as a submission.','', 'Commands from the existing project root (retain the audited immutable V1 caches):','```sh','.venv/bin/python outputs/run1_investigation/source/diagnose.py','.venv/bin/python outputs/run1_investigation/source/explain.py','.venv/bin/python outputs/run1_investigation/source/flexible_flow.py','.venv/bin/python outputs/run1_investigation/source/feature_checks.py','.venv/bin/python outputs/run1_investigation/source/supplement.py','.venv/bin/python outputs/run1_investigation/source/study.py','.venv/bin/python outputs/run1_investigation/source/report.py','```','The supplied public metadata snapshot is a provenance input to diagnose.py, not a model input. Environment matches solution/requirements.txt, Python 3.12.13; no new ML dependencies. Models and per-transaction local error/OOF files stay local and are excluded from the research evidence ZIP.']
